{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"da88d47b-b3e6-4617-b2d1-2d87cfc847aa","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root cause of the test failures was an unnecessary `i++` in the escaped backslash handler inside [`readString`](file:///tmp/agentcap-agent-trial-71366550/acap-bench-2523972121/lexer/lexer.go#L91-L120) in [lexer/lexer.go](file:///tmp/agentcap-agent-trial-71366550/acap-bench-2523972121/lexer/lexer.go#L110):\n\n- When encountering an escape sequence `\\\\`, `i` was already incremented to point to the second backslash.\n- Inside `case '\\\\'`, another `i++` was executed in addition to the loop's own increment, skipping the character immediately following the escaped backslash or advancing past the closing quote (causing unterminated string errors).\n\n### Changes Made\n- Removed the extra `i++` inside `case '\\\\'` in [`lexer/lexer.go`](file:///tmp/agentcap-agent-trial-71366550/acap-bench-2523972121/lexer/lexer.go#L109-L112).\n- Verified that all unit tests across the repository pass (`go test -count=1 ./...`).\n","duration_seconds":33.045320362,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":104437,"output_tokens":3207,"thinking_tokens":2003,"cache_read_tokens":64990,"total_tokens":107644}}}
